"\n"
"Also honoured on the OUTPUT side, where it names the period a supply was actually declared in rather than its tax point — a § 42 correction is declared when the corrective document reaches the customer, and a document entered late is declared in the period of entry. Empty is the normal case there and the tax point governs, so a document raised in Odoo behaves exactly as before.\n"
"\n"
"Leave empty for the normal case, where a bill is booked in the period it is claimed: the accounting date is then used. It matters for documents booked in one period and claimed in another, and for accounting history imported from a system that records the two dates separately."
msgstr ""

